    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Respondent",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "df54ad0cd6252e33e73d84728290acc531876ba010acd1486a863993b824b19c",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-df54ad0cd625-0001-0008"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 29,
                "start": 29
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Respondent, when the \u00a7\u202f924(c) offense is ongoing and the firearm is discharged, the mandatory minimum sentence applies."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Respondent",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "df54ad0cd6252e33e73d84728290acc531876ba010acd1486a863993b824b19c",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-df54ad0cd625-0001-0010"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 31,
                "start": 31
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Respondent, if a teller grabs the gun from the robber and it discharges while the offense continues, that counts as a discharge under the statute."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Respondent",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "df54ad0cd6252e33e73d84728290acc531876ba010acd1486a863993b824b19c",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-df54ad0cd625-0001-0013"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 34,
                "start": 34
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Respondent, congress intended a mens\u2011rea element for the discharge provision."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Respondent",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "df54ad0cd6252e33e73d84728290acc531876ba010acd1486a863993b824b19c",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-df54ad0cd625-0001-0014"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 35,
                "start": 35
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Respondent, both the robber and the teller engaged in inherently dangerous activity."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Respondent Position",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": "The respondent contends that a discharge occurring while the \u00a7\u202f924(c) offense is ongoing triggers the mandatory minimum, that a teller\u2019s discharge counts, and that Congress intended a mens\u2011rea element and recognized the dangerous nature of the conduct.",
